  OK   A population of 10,000 is roughly where drift permanently stops for an animal like us, the size of the population below which a neutral allele can still cross the whole population by chance in all the generations its lineage will ever have, and above which it cannot.
  OK   4Nₑ < G, where G is the number of generations of the lineage concerned.
  OK   effective ceiling falls to about ten thousand individuals.
  OK   Nₑ = (4N − 2) / (Vₖ + 2)
